course: dictionary
lesson: 10569
title: Unconsciousness
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Look at the word in pieces. «Un-» means not, «conscious» means awake and aware, and «-ness» turns it into a noun, a name for a state. So unconsciousness is the state of not being awake and not able to notice anything. Someone can be in unconsciousness after a bad fall or when they faint.
explain: In a story, a character might slip into unconsciousness after a blow to the head. This is serious. If someone falls into unconsciousness, get an adult straight away and call the emergency number: 999 in the UK and Ireland, 911 in the USA and Canada, 000 in Australia, or 111 in New Zealand. Only use first aid such as the recovery position if you have been properly taught how.
explain: The word can also be used in a gentler way. «Inside, the people have the natural grace which goes with perfect unconsciousness of observation.» Here it means not being aware that anyone is watching. Because they do not know they are being watched, they look natural. Context helps you see which meaning fits.
fact: Unconsciousness means being not awake and not able to notice anything.
fact: «Unconscious» is the adjective: a person who is not awake is unconscious.
fact: Unconsciousness is an uncountable noun, so you say «unconsciousness», not «unconsciousnesses».
fact: If someone falls into unconsciousness, call the emergency number and get an adult to help.
fact: In «perfect unconsciousness of observation», the word means not knowing that anyone is watching.
exercise: «Inside, the people have the natural grace which goes with perfect unconsciousness of observation.» What does unconsciousness of observation mean? | Being very tired after a long day | Shouting loudly at a crowd | Staring hard at a painting | *Not knowing that anyone is watching
exercise: After the fall, Sam lay still and could not be woken. He was in unconsciousness. What does unconsciousness mean? | Fully dressed and ready for school | *Not awake and not able to notice anything | Wide awake and running about | Laughing loudly with friends
exercise: Someone falls into unconsciousness at the park. What should you do first? | *Get an adult and call the emergency number | Leave them alone to sleep it off | Take a photo and post it online | Give them a drink and walk away
test:
Which word is the noun for the state of being unconscious? | unconscious | *unconsciousness | conscious | consciously
After a bad fall, the boy slipped into unconsciousness. What happened to him? | He was on the ground, wide awake and shouting | *He was not awake and could not notice anything | He was giggling at a joke | He was reading a book quietly
exam: Which meaning is closest to unconsciousness? | *Not being awake and not able to notice anything | Happiness and excitement | Awareness of everything around you | Quick movement from place to place
